ags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "spells", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "A shift (of work); (rare) a set of workers responsible for a specific turn of labour.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal) A definite period (of work or other activity).", "tags": ["informal"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "A chap named Eleazir Kendrick and I had chummed in together the summer afore and built a fish-weir and shanty at Setuckit Point, down Orham way. For a spell we done pretty well. Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand.", "reference": "1913, Joseph C[rosby] Lincoln, chapter I, in Mr. Pratt’s Patients, New York, N.Y.; London: D[aniel] Appleton and Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "I had a job in the great North Woods / Workin' as a cook for a spell / But I never did like it all that much / And one day the ax just fell", "reference": "1975, Bob Dylan, “Tangled Up in Blue”:"}, {"text": "Despite his ill-fated spell at Anfield, he received a warm reception from the same Liverpool fans he struggled to win over before being sacked midway through last season.", "reference": "2012 April 22, Sam Sheringham, “Liverpool 0-1 West Brom”, in BBC Sport:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(colloquial) An indefinite period of time (usually with a qualifier); by extension, a relatively short distance.", "tags": ["colloquial"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Even Mrs. Harker seems to lose sight of her trouble for whole spells. [...] When he had spoken, Mina's long spell of silence made me look at her.", "reference": "1897, Bram Stoker, chapter 24, in Dracula, HTML edition:"}, {"text": "So after a short spell in the brass foundry the wisest course was to follow with a similar period in the steel foundry, where much important work was done, including the manufacture of centres for wheels.", "reference": "1944 November and December, A Former Pupil, “Some Memories of Crewe Works—II”, in Railway Magazine, page 343:"}, {"text": "[...] Class 37s became synonymous with the depot, and over the years more than a third of the class had a spell allocated to the shed.", "reference": "2020 June 17, John Crosse, “Thornaby's traction transition”, in Rail, page 65:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "кратко време"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "陣 /阵"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "jakso"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "moment"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "épisode"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "kurze Periode"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Weile"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Weilchen"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "Zeitdauer"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "περίοδος"}, {"language": {"code": "ia", "name": "Interlingua"}, "word": "breve periodo"}, {"language": {"code": "ia", "name": "Interlingua"}, "word": "intervallo"}, {"language": {"code": "ga", "name": "Irish"}, "word": "tamall"}, {"language": {"code": "ga", "name": "Irish"}, "word": "scaitheamh"}, {"language": {"code": "ga", "name": "Irish"}, "word": "seal"}, {"language": {"code": "ko", "name": "Korean"}, "word": "한참"}, {"language": {"code": "ko", "name": "Korean"}, "word": "한동안"}, {"language": {"code": "lv", "name": "Latvian"}, "word": "īss laika sprīdis"}, {"language": {"code": "mi", "name": "Māori"}, "word": "tūāmoe"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "krótki okres"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "breve período"}, {"langua